## Phase 3 — Note Types (extend data model)

Introduce a discriminated union on `Note`. **Default existing docs to `type: 'task'`** for backward compatibility.

```typescript
// app/screens/types.ts
export type NoteType = 'task' | 'checklist' | 'reminder' | 'recurring';

export interface BaseNote {
  id: string;
  type: NoteType;
  title?: string;
  completed: boolean;
  createdAt: string;
  category?: string;
  userId?: string;
  startDate?: string;
  endDate?: string;
}

export interface TaskNote extends BaseNote {
  type: 'task';
  note: string;
}

export interface ChecklistNote extends BaseNote {
  type: 'checklist';
  items: { id: string; text: string; checked: boolean }[];
}

export interface ReminderNote extends BaseNote {
  type: 'reminder';
  note?: string;
  remindAt: string; // ISO datetime
}

export interface RecurringNote extends BaseNote {
  type: 'recurring';
  note: string;
  recurrence: 'daily' | 'weekly' | 'monthly' | 'custom';
  recurrenceDays?: number[]; // 0=Sun for weekly
}

export type Note = TaskNote | ChecklistNote | ReminderNote | RecurringNote;
```

### 3.1 Task (current behavior)
- Keep as default; no migration needed beyond adding `type` field on read

### 3.2 Checklist
- QuickAdd: paste or add multiple lines → checklist items
- NoteItem: show `2/5` progress badge
- NoteDetail: reorder items, add/remove sub-items
- Complete parent when all items checked (configurable in settings)

### 3.3 Reminder
- Time picker in QuickAdd (not just date)
- Notification at `remindAt` (extend `notificationService`)
- NoteItem: clock icon + relative time ("in 3h")

### 3.4 Recurring — **partial (flat model)**

**Done (without full `RecurringNote` union):**
- `Note.recurrence?: 'weekly' | 'biweekly'` on flat type + Firestore mapper
- QuickAdd `SegmentedControl`: None | Weekly | 2 weeks (single-day only when repeating)
- `noteDates.ts`: `noteOccursOnDay`, `getNoteCalendarDays`, `advanceRecurrenceDates`, `formatRecurrenceLabel`
- Calendar marks + agenda show future recurring occurrences
- Complete recurring task → advance `startDate`/`endDate` by 7 or 14 days (stay active)
- `NoteItem` shows "Repeats weekly" / "Repeats every 2 weeks"

**Still pending (full §3.4):**
- Discriminated `RecurringNote` type with `daily` | `monthly` | `custom` + `recurrenceDays`
- Recurring icon on calendar / NoteItem
- Edit recurrence in `NoteDetail`
- Settings: default recurrence for new notes

### 3.5 Type picker in QuickAdd
- Segmented control: Task | Checklist | Reminder | Recurring
- Remember last-used type per user (AsyncStorage)
- Render type-specific fields only (progressive disclosure)

### 3.6 Firestore migration
- Add `type` on write for all new notes
- `mapDocToNote` / `subscribeToNotes` mapper: `type: data.type ?? 'task'`
- Optional one-time admin script to backfill `type` on existing docs

